* TR-808 voicing board: the metallic source's mixer and band-passes (service notes p.13). The six
* HD14584 Schmitt oscillators (IC1, on the 4.7 V rail Q9 makes) are inputs o1-o6 (their square
* waves); R50, R48, R46, R39, R37, R35 (120k each) mix them into R53. IC3b picks out the high band
* (bridged T, about 7.1 kHz) for the cymbal's Q16/Q17 and the hats' Q27/Q30, IC3a the low band
* (about 3.4 kHz) for the cymbal's Q18. Outputs: hi (IC3b pin 7), lo (IC3a pin 1).
VO1 o1 0 input o1
VO2 o2 0 input o2
VO3 o3 0 input o3
VO4 o4 0 input o4
VO5 o5 0 input o5
VO6 o6 0 input o6
R50 o1 mix 120k
R48 o2 mix 120k
R46 o3 mix 120k
R39 o4 mix 120k
R37 o5 mix 120k
R35 o6 mix 120k
R53 mix 0 1k
* high band, IC3b
C11 mix c11 0.001u
R55 c11 n3b 22k
C15 n3b m3b 0.0033u
C16 m3b hi 0.0033u
R58 m3b 0 560
R59 n3b hi 82k
X3B 0 n3b hi opamp {gbw}
* low band, IC3a
C10 mix c10 0.0033u
R52 c10 n3a 33k
C13 n3a m3a 0.0068u
C14 m3a lo 0.0068u
R56 m3a 0 560
R57 n3a lo 82k
X3A 0 n3a lo opamp {gbw}
.output hi hi
.output lo lo
